a) (symbol? a))\n463:    (and (or (keyword? b) (symbol? b))\n479:    (set? a) (and (set? b)\n518:   sign counts, and every NaN is the one canonical NaN), within decimal the\n543:   namespace and name fields, lists and vectors alike (README ruling A6)\n544:   element by element, maps and sets by members, metadata ignored, any other\n545:   value as itself. A caller keys a host map or set by it to get\n554:    (or (keyword? x) (symbol? x)) [::identifier (identifier-key x)]\n557:    (set? x) (into #{} (map content-key) x)\n566:   width is not significant, and canonical NaNs are equal (every NaN has\n567:   the one canonical encoding). Collections recurse the way equiv does,\n568:   metadata ignored. Unlike equiv, (content= 1 1.0) is false.\"\n582:;; Encode: direct canonical CBOR byte writer (RFC 8949) over dao.host.*\n611:   contents one level deeper, so a list frame (tag, [name items]) costs\n637:  \"Emits canonical shortest header bytes for major type `major` (0..7)\n657:        (bytes/set! out 0 (bit-or major-byte 26))\n665:        (bytes/set! out 0 (bit-or major-byte 27))\n684:(defn- compare-canonical-bytes\n686:   a proper prefix sorting first (RFC 8949 canonical order).\"\n777:  \"Encodes [key value] pairs (value nil for set elements), members at depth d,\n778:   refusing duplicate canonical encodings (dup-class) and portable-equality\n781:  [pairs set? dup-class d]\n784:                            vb (when-not set? (value-bytes v d))]\n787:    (when (< (count (set (map second wired))) (count wired))\n799:        sorted (sort #(compare-canonical-bytes (first %1) (first %2)) wired)\n804:(defn- set-bytes\n812:        sorted (sort #(compare-canonical-bytes (first %1) (first %2)) wired)\n818:(defn- meta-bytes\n820:   content starting at that depth. If x carries metadata that survives\n821:   stripping, a with-meta frame sits at d and x's content moves two\n822:   levels deeper (tag, [meta value]). Stripped values are validated\n823:   first (ruling A9); a metadata map carrying its own metadata is\n826:  (let [m (meta x)]\n829:      (do (when (some? (meta m))\n830:            (refuse :malformed-frame \"metadata map carries metadata\"))\n837:              (let [name-bytes (host text/utf8-encode \"clojure/with-meta\")\n868:(defn- list-bytes\n869:  \"Tag 27 at depth d over [\\\"dao.jing/list\\\" items]: items at d+3.\"\n872:  (let [tag-name-bytes (host text/utf8-encode \"dao.jing/list\")\n883:  \"The canonical CBOR bytes of one value whose outermost item sits at depth d,\n893:    (symbol? x) (meta-bytes x d #(identifier-bytes \"dao.jing/symbol\" x %))\n903:    (map? x) (meta-bytes x d #(map-bytes x %))\n904:    (vector? x) (meta-bytes x d (fn [d]\n908:    (set? x) (meta-bytes x d #(set-bytes x %))\n909:    (or (list? x) (seq? x)) (meta-bytes x d #(list-bytes x %))\n914:  \"The canonical CBOR payload bytes of one supported value (byte[] on the\n930:  \"Order two supported values by their canonical encodings: the shorter\n931:   encoding first, then unsigned bytewise (note: canonical map and set encoding\n1120:    (when (< (count (set raws)) (count items))\n1147:    \"dao.jing/list\"\n1149:      ;; ClojureDart's list constructor attaches call-site metadata;\n1150:      ;; a decoded list carries none until a with-meta frame adds it.\n1151:      #?(:cljd (with-meta (apply list (map #(item->value bs %) (:value p))) nil)\n1152:         :default (apply list (map #(item->value bs %) (:value p))))\n1153:      (refuse :malformed-frame \"list payload is not an array\"))\n1155:    (\"dao.jing/keyword\" \"dao.jing/symbol\")\n1167:          (symbol ns (:value name-item)))))\n1175:    \"clojure/with-meta\"\n1178:                                      \"with-meta payload is not [meta value]\"))\n1182:        (refuse :malformed-frame \"metadata is not a map\"))\n1183:      (when (some? (meta m))\n1184:        (refuse :malformed-frame \"metadata map carries metadata\"))\n1185:      (when-not (and (or (vector? v) (map? v) (set? v) (list? v) (symbol? v))\n1186:                     (nil? (meta v)))\n1188:                \"metadata target is not a bare collection or symbol\"))\n\n\n(defn- manifest\n  [id language]\n  {:yang.frontend/id id,\n   :yang.frontend/spi 1,\n   :yang.frontend/revision \"legacy-1\",\n   :yang.frontend/language language,\n   :yang.frontend/grammar {:yang.grammar/package \"none\",\n                           :yang.grammar/entries {:module \"program\"},\n                           :yang.grammar/export-profile :yang.cst/v1},\n   :yang.frontend/options-schema :segment/none,\n   :yang.frontend/lowering-profile :segment/legacy,\n   :yang.frontend/runtime-profile :segment/legacy,\n   :yang.frontend/support-profile :segment/legacy})\n\n\n(defn clojure-manifest\n  \"The Clojure frontend's manifest. Its coverage promise changed under\n   the call-site occurrence contract C1 — every final `:application`\n   occurrence carries `:yang/call-site` in the frontend-metadata side\n   table, finalized over the post-expansion tree that executes and\n   retained beside a published module's manifest — and that promise is\n   a support claim, so the revision and the support profile name it;\n   the shared legacy profiles no longer describe this frontend.\"\n  []\n  (assoc (manifest :yang/clojure :clojure)\n         :yang.frontend/revision \"c1-1\"\n         :yang.frontend/support-profile :yang.clojure/c1))\n\n\n(defn- clojure-lower\n  [forms]\n  (if (= 1 (count forms))\n    (yang.clojure/compile (first forms))\n    (yang.clojure/compile-program forms)))\n\n\n(defn- antlr-manifest\n  []\n  (assoc (manifest :yang/python :python)\n         :yang.frontend/revision \"f4\"\n         :yang.frontend/grammar\n         {:yang.grammar/package \"python3\",\ntest/yang/latte_oracle/h3_2_a_verify.clj\ntest/yang/latte_oracle/h3_3_a_verify.clj\ntest/yang/safepoint_test.cljc\ntest/yang/typescript_callsite_test.cljc\ntest/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc\ntest/yang/call/depth_probe_test.clj\ntest/yang/call/php_exception_test.clj\ntest/yang/call/exception_probes.clj\ntest/yang/call/conformance.clj\ntest/yang/call/exception_legs.clj\ntest/yang/call/exception_contract_test.clj\ntest/yang/call/exception_contract.clj\ntest/yang/call/python_exception_test.clj\ntest/yang/call/exception_source_test.clj\ntest/yang/call/conformance_test.clj\ntest/yang/frontend_test.cljc\ntest/yang/php/antlr/p5b2_lifecycle_test.clj\ntest/yang/php/antlr/programs_p7b.cljc\ntest/yang/php/antlr/scope_test.clj\ntest/yang/php/antlr/eval_coordinator_test.clj\ntest/yang/php/antlr/builtin_surfaces_test.clj\ntest/yang/php/antlr/linked_harness.cljc\ntest/yang/php/antlr/programs_p3b.cljc\ntest/yang/php/antlr/eval_publication_test.clj\ntest/yang/php/antlr/programs_p9.cljc\ntest/yang/php/antlr/generators_test.clj\ntest/yang/php/antlr/portable_harness.cljc\ntest/yang/php/antlr/eval_bridge_test.clj\ntest/yang/php/antlr/programs_p5.cljc\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_test.clj\ntest/yang/php/antlr/eval_scope_cleanup_test.clj\ntest/yang/php/antlr/programs_p4.cljc\ntest/yang/php/antlr/programs_p8.cljc\ntest/yang/php/antlr/cst_test.clj\ntest/yang/php/antlr/ticks_test.clj\ntest/yang/php/antlr/include_test.clj\ntest/yang/php/antlr/zz_probe2_test.clj\ntest/yang/php/antlr/zz_probe3_test.clj\ntest/yang/php/antlr/request_context_test.clj\ntest/yang/php/antlr/eval_transport_test.clj\ntest/yang/php/antlr/eval_emitter_test.clj\ntest/yang/php/antlr/programs.cljc\ntest/yang/php/antlr/siteset_test.clj\ntest/yang/php/antlr/exceptions_test.clj\ntest/yang/php/antlr/p8_corpus_test.clj\ntest/yang/php/antlr/programs_p6.cljc\ntest/yang/php/antlr/zz_probe_test.clj\ntest/yang/php/antlr/permutations.cljc\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj\ntest/yang/php/antlr/eval_admission_test.clj\ntest/yang/php/antlr/class_model_test.cljc\ntest/yang/php/antlr/phpt.clj\ntest/yang/php/antlr/programs_p5b2.cljc\ntest/yang/php/antlr/prelude_test.cljc\ntest/yang/php/antlr/packets.cljc\ntest/yang/php/antlr/safepoint_test.clj\ntest/yang/php/antlr/packets_p3b.cljc\ntest/yang/php/antlr/finali